# The venv this Containerfile builds ships no pip (see v1.0.2: pip is deleted
# from /app/venv before the runtime COPY, since nothing at runtime needs it —
# ENTRYPOINT execs /app/venv/bin/python directly, never pip).
#
# What remains is pip's OWN vendored copy of these libraries, baked into the
# runtime base image itself (quay.io/hummingbird/python:3.13, not built by
# this repo) at /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-26.2.dist-info.
# Confirmed by extracting that base image's layers directly: pip 26.2's own
# pip/_vendor/vendor.txt pins msgpack==1.1.2 and setuptools==70.3.0, matching
# these findings exactly.
#
# Not fixable here: the versions are frozen inside pip itself, and this
# repo's runtime stage is distroless (no shell, no RUN) — there is no way for
# this Containerfile to reach into an inherited FROM layer and delete files
# from it. A real fix requires Hummingbird shipping a base image without a
# stale vendored pip.
#
# Not reachable: that /usr/local install isn't on PATH (ENV PATH puts
# /app/venv/bin first) and nothing in this image ever invokes pip at
# runtime — there's no lazy install, no package-index call, no code path
# that touches pip/_vendor at all after the image is built.
#
#   HIGH  GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964  msgpack 1.1.2      OOB read / crash on Unpacker reuse
#   HIGH  CVE-2025-47273       setuptools 70.3.0  path traversal in PackageIndex
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2025-47273
